WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 7.3 · Brand, Identity & Image
Brand personality, voice and tone

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your voice stays the same; your tone changes with the situation. Write both down early.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
Brand personality describes your initiative as if it were a person. Voice is how that personality sounds in words, and it stays the same; tone changes with the situation.

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Personality, voice and tone

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:34.907
Personality: Three or four traits, drawn from your values, that audiences would recognise. For example: Our bakery: warm, encouraging and practical.

6
00:00:34.907 --> 00:00:44.756
Voice: How the traits sound, each written as “this, not that”. For example: “Encouraging, not patronising”: we celebrate effort, never “even you can do it”.

7
00:00:44.756 --> 00:00:54.604
Tone: Shifts with the situation while the voice stays the same. For example: Serious when answering a complaint; joyful when sharing the first trainee’s certificate.

8
00:00:54.604 --> 00:01:05.281
Word list: Words you use, words you avoid and how you describe people. For example: Say “young people”, not “at-risk youth”; say “trainees”, not “beneficiaries”.

9
00:01:05.681 --> 00:01:06.281
Why it matters

10
00:01:06.281 --> 00:01:11.215
1. Anyone who writes for you can sound like you.

11
00:01:11.215 --> 00:01:16.148
2. Your voice stops living only in the founders’ heads.

12
00:01:16.148 --> 00:01:22.452
3. Respectful words protect the dignity of the people you serve.

13
00:01:22.852 --> 00:01:23.452
Where you will use it

14
00:01:23.452 --> 00:01:28.756
1. Your guidelines, so volunteers and partners write in your voice.

15
00:01:28.756 --> 00:01:32.207
2. Your messages, posts and newsletters.

16
00:01:32.207 --> 00:01:37.400
3. Your stories, told without pity or stereotypes.

17
00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:38.400
What to avoid

18
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.593
Choosing traits your audiences would not recognise.

19
00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:48.637
Language that reduces people to their problems or shows them as helpless.

20
00:01:48.637 --> 00:01:54.200
Never testing the voice on a real message.

21
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.600
You define your personality, voice, tone and word list.

22
00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.600
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.200
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
